---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="What Sky Workbench is and how its posts are structured.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-title">
      <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
      <h1>A workbench for the sky</h1>
      <div class="dim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
    <section class="section prose">
      <p>
        Sky Workbench is for people who would rather build the thing than read about it. Every post is
        meant to be reproducible: what the goal was, what it took, what happened, and the files to try it
        yourself.
      </p>
      <h2>How posts are structured</h2>
      <p>
        Each post is a numbered drawing (DWG-001, DWG-002, …) in the order it was published. It opens with a
        title block: the goal, difficulty, time, cost and a bill of materials. Then comes the build or the
        analysis itself, including what went wrong, and links to the files and code so you can repeat it.
      </p>
      <h2>Red mode</h2>
      <p>
        The <code>◐ Red</code> button in the header turns the whole site red so you can read it at the
        eyepiece without wrecking your night vision.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Replace this section with your email, GitHub or Mastodon handle.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
